window.__PROFILE.facts = [{"n": 1, "text": "if you want to skip the combat challenge from Fremennik Trials, Thorvald says he'll vote for you if you bring him 5 sardines! there's even special dialogue if you use the sardines on him, but he was \"only joking\" the whole time :(", "page": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "In 2003, spaghetti code from Gertrude's Cat broke the \"desert heat\" effect in RuneScape Classic \u2013 and it never, ever worked again", "page": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "the font used for the original RUNESCAPE logo is also used for the signage of nearly half of all Asian-themed restaurants in the United States", "page": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "ever wonder why some monsters drop nature talismans but others drop chaos? Monsters in \"underground\" areas are supposed to give chaos, but the game's definition of \"underground\" hasn't changed since 2003, and is broken in all sorts of fun ways", "page": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "if you use the Ring of Endurance on the archpriest unicorn in Hallowed Sepulchre, it unlocks secret dialogue explaining where the ring came from", "page": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "due to a series of unfortunate coincidences, the \"yellow circle\" shape from Eyes of Glouphrie has never been obtainable", "page": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "the level-1 citizens of Miscellania have weird overhead dialogue, only when fighting back against players. This some of the most rarely-seen text in the game, because they have 1 HP, and nobody kills them because they cost 6% Miscellania favour", "page": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "the steepest walkable terrain in the game is the hill between the waterfall and the Grand Tree, which goes from the lowest possible height value (0) to the highest (255) in a single tile", "page": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "there's an inaccessible ladder in a dark part of the Smoke Dungeon, two floors up. it's conjectured to be one of the few things that made it into the game from the version of Desert Treasure made by \"the intern\"", "page": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "there's a single cave goblin miner in the Dorgeshuun mine that still uses the janky pre-2007 goblin chatheads! you have to do something slightly clever to get it to show up", "page": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "the weirdest Agility training method I've ever heard of: Rogues Den gives you 12 XP per level that gets drained(??) which means the \"cheese strat\" is to run back and forth on the obstacle that drains your Agility level until you get kicked out. it's good for about 22k XP an hour", "page": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "did you know there used to be a boat that took you from Port Khazard to Brimhaven for 30 gp? \"Docky\" inexplicably wasn't included in the RuneScape Classic->RS2 transition, although his boat was (and still exists in OSRS today)! We think the 2004-era devs just forgot about him :(", "page": null}];
